<worksheet xmlns="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main"><sheetPr><outlinePr summaryBelow="1" summaryRight="1"/><pageSetUpPr/></sheetPr><dimension ref="A1:C16"/><sheetViews><sheetView showGridLines="0" workbookViewId="0"><pane ySplit="1" topLeftCell="A2" activePane="bottomLeft" state="frozen"/><selection pane="bottomLeft" activeCell="A1" sqref="A1"/></sheetView></sheetViews><sheetFormatPr baseColWidth="8" defaultRowHeight="15"/><cols><col width="30" customWidth="1" min="1" max="1"/><col width="26" customWidth="1" min="2" max="2"/><col width="56" customWidth="1" min="3" max="3"/></cols><sheetData><row r="1" ht="28" customHeight="1"><c r="A1" s="10" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Scope to Avoid</t></is></c><c r="B1" s="10" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Who Already Owns It</t></is></c><c r="C1" s="10" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Why AiForm Should Not Compete Here</t></is></c></row><row r="2" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A2" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Full procure-to-pay</t></is></c><c r="B2" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Coupa, SAP Ariba</t></is></c><c r="C2" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Mature global enterprise systems with deep ERP integration already embedded at major mines (Sibanye, Thungela). Years and significant capital behind each.</t></is></c></row><row r="3" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A3" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>ERP</t></is></c><c r="B3" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Coupa, SAP Ariba, mine-internal systems</t></is></c><c r="C3" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Not a product AiForm has any structural advantage building; wrong layer of the stack entirely.</t></is></c></row><row r="4" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A4" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Invoice processing</t></is></c><c r="B4" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Coupa, SAP Ariba, mine finance systems</t></is></c><c r="C4" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Downstream of procurement decisioning; high integration burden for low differentiation.</t></is></c></row><row r="5" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A5" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Purchase-order management</t></is></c><c r="B5" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Coupa, SAP Ariba</t></is></c><c r="C5" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Same rationale &#8212; transactional plumbing owned by incumbents with existing mine integrations.</t></is></c></row><row r="6" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A6" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Mine inventory systems</t></is></c><c r="B6" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Mine-internal / specialist mining software</t></is></c><c r="C6" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Entirely outside AiForm's compliance/verification core competency.</t></is></c></row><row r="7" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A7" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Generic ESD (Enterprise &amp; Supplier Development) management</t></is></c><c r="B7" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>ESDHub, B1SA/B1LINK, SCNet</t></is></c><c r="C7" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Crowded category with established players; not mining-specific enough to differentiate.</t></is></c></row><row r="8" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A8" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Standalone Mining Charter calculator</t></is></c><c r="B8" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>MineVendorHub (positioning), internal mining company tools</t></is></c><c r="C8" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Too narrow a wedge &#8212; a calculator alone doesn't solve opportunity discovery or verification.</t></is></c></row><row r="9" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A9" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Another general supplier directory</t></is></c><c r="B9" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>SCNet, B1SA/B1LINK, MEMSA</t></is></c><c r="C9" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Directory alone is a commodity; several credible, established directories already exist in the SA market.</t></is></c></row><row r="10" ht="40" customHeight="1"><c r="A10" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Reverse / forward auction tools</t></is></c><c r="B10" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>SCNet</t></is></c><c r="C10" s="7" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Niche, capital- and trust-intensive feature; not aligned with AiForm's supplier-first entry strategy.</t></is></c></row><row r="12" ht="24" customHeight="1"><c r="A12" s="3" t="inlineStr"><is><t>Where AiForm should focus instead</t></is></c></row><row r="13" ht="18" customHeight="1"><c r="A13" s="4" t="inlineStr"><is><t>"Where can this particular company realistically win work?" &#8212; the Mining Supplier Passport (compliance + Mining Charter + host-community + SHEQ profile) combined with an eligibility/match engine and gap analysis, routing qualified suppliers into whichever buyer system (Coupa, Ariba, SCNet, proprietary portal) the opportunity actually lives on. This is the one capability cluster (automated % match + gap analysis) that no reviewed competitor currently offers.</t></is></c></row><row r="14" ht="18" customHeight="1"></row><row r="15" ht="18" customHeight="1"></row><row r="16" ht="18" customHeight="1"></row></sheetData><mergeCells count="2"><mergeCell ref="A12:C12"/><mergeCell ref="A13:C16"/></mergeCells><pageMargins left="0.75" right="0.75" top="1" bottom="1" header="0.5" footer="0.5"/></worksheet>